## 2. Google Sheets Schema & Column Reference

The detail page queries three different sheets. The table below lists the columns extracted and how they are merged:

### A. Sheet: `PO consolidated data`
Holds transactional line items. Filters all rows where `comms_group_id` matches the URL parameter.

| Sheet Column Name | JSON Output Key | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `po_number` | `header.poNumber` | Purchase Order number (displayed in header). |
| `comms_group_id` | `header.commsGroupId` | Unique communications group identifier. |
| `po_status` | `header.status` | Transaction status (e.g., "Open"). |
| `issue_date` | `header.issueDate` | Date the purchase order was issued. |
| `po_line_key` | `lineItems[].poLineKey` | Unique line item key (e.g. `PO12345_1`). |
| `po_line_item` | `lineItems[].lineItem` | Line item index number. |
| `material_code` | `lineItems[].materialCode` | Part or item number. |
| `material_name` | `lineItems[].materialName` | Description of the material. |
| `quantity` | `lineItems[].quantity` | Order quantity value. |
| `unit_of_measure` | `lineItems[].uom` | Order unit of measure (e.g., EA). |
| `ship_by_date_delivery_1` | `lineItems[].shipBy` | Requested ship-by date. |
| `deliver_by_date_delivery_1` | `lineItems[].deliverBy` | Requested delivery-by date. |
| `carrier` | `lineItems[].carrier` | Shipping carrier name (if shipped). |
| `trackingNumber` | `lineItems[].trackingNumber` | Shipment tracking identifier. |

